WEBVTT

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.380
It's a depressing sky, isn't it?

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.260
What? It's more than just depressing!

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.680
We were up all night, and they're making
us go shopping straight from the work site!

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.430
Jeez, this is the worst!

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:02.970
Oh, it lit up again.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:07.850
I'm sorry. I said that
I could do it by myself, but...

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.100
What are you talking about?

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.730
It's obvious that you
couldn't do it on your own!

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.020
But...

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.400
Oh,the phone!

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.280
Are you all right, Azmaria?

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.900
Yes, absolutely...

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.870
Oh, you just sit still!
Chrono, answer the phone!

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:22.740
Are you sure?

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.410
Can't you tell by looking? I'm driving!

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.500
Hello?
Minister Remington? Rosette is currently...

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.050
Hello, this is Rosette.
Is something the matter?

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.090
No, no, it's super okay.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.550
Grand Central Station at 5 o'clock, right?

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:43.890
Yes... yes... All right, see you later.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:48.810
Oh, today I'm super lucky!

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:49.810
What's going on?

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:52.560
I'm going to the train station
to get Minister Remington.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.730
What, right now?

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.820
For him to choose me personally...

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:59.150
Does this mean he's
finally realized my appeal?

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.990
Now that that's been decided,
I'd better hurry!

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.450
That's impossible
with all of these packages!

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.120
Which is why we're
going back to the convent first!

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.960
Although if I left
you here, it would be just right.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.630
Wait a second!

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.720
Was that all right?

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:30.980
This has become bothersome...

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.200
What in the world is he doing?

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.200
Being on time is part of the mission too.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.450
Mama...

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.370
Where's my snack?

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.500
Just be patient for a little longer.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.630
Grandma is baking a cake for us at home.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:58.250
But I've already been patient.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.840
He's not going to come.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.640
You were supposed to receive this, right?

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.970
Who are you?

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:11.640
A servant for the group
that you're investigating.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.850
What happened to him?

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.310
Oh, you should praise him.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:19.190
He was sniffing around,
just as you ordered him to.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.480
Where is he?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.740
I ate him.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.280
There's not a scrap
of him left. Thanks for the meal.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.220
I'm here.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.810
Here, here...

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:57.190
This is because you're a dangerous man.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.610
So they're supposed to be hostages?

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:05.740
Now, hand over that dangerous thing.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.410
Let's do business.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.960
I think I'm going to bite my tongue.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.000
Come on, let's hurry up and move the stuff!

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.000
Okay!

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.260
Are you all right, Azmaria?

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.340
I fell down.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.600
Want me to carry it?

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.770
No! I can handle this much.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:34.850
Maybe I should...

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.890
I'm going to do it!

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:40.270
Oh, it doesn't matter who
does it, hurry up and get it moved!

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:43.610
How can you say that?

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.200
I... I just want to help everyone...

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.080
Well, that is... You don't have to cry.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.830
Then please do your best
in carrying them in, Azmaria.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:55.830
Okay!

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:04.800
And this is all of it.
Can you handle it from here, Azmaria?

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.970
Yes, please leave it to me.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.340
Oh, welcome back. That was fast.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.970
A reason for me to hurry came up.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.140
What?

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.060
What <i>is</i> this?!

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:23.690
The wheat is soaked
with water! We can't use it that way!

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:27.650
Oh, shut up. You can still use half of it!

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:30.320
Well, this is because I fell down earlier.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.780
You were a little carsick
because Rosette drives too fast, right?

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.950
Wait a second, Chrono,
are you saying that this is my fault?

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.040
Well, you know...

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:44.000
What, again?! You have got to
learn to drive a car properly already.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.800
Chrono and Azmaria won't
be able to take much more.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.840
That's right, I heard that just recently

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:53.010
Rosette got distracted by
a fruit cart and almost had an accident!

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:56.180
What? Didn't she run into the cart?

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:00.310
That's not it. She tried to avoid the cart
and crashed into a bakery across the street,

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:03.020
and both the shop
and the car took serious damage.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:07.780
We can't even ask Rosette to go shopping.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:14.830
That's all you have to say to someone who
took the trouble to go shopping in the rain?!

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:19.500
Rosette, calm down already.
Hey, weren't you in a hurry?

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.080
That's right, I don't have the time for this.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.510
Aren't you lucky?

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:39.220
Wait a minute,
did she hear anything that we just said?

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:42.520
She's in such a hurry.
Just where is Rosette going?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.730
She's going to the train station
to pick up Minister Remington.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.070
Oh, how strange.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:50.740
Minister Remington
went out in a car himself.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.250
Safe! Made it in time.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:06.380
All right.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.380
It's about time for the princess to arrive.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:14.340
Before that, let me
ask something of all of you.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.470
There shouldn't be
anything that you need to ask.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.600
Are you working for Aion?

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:27.440
What are you planning
on doing with Rosette?

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.900
Nothing, I'm just going
to have her come with me.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.950
That person needs her.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.280
That person?

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:00.140
Lord Joshua...

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.520
It will do your body harm
to be exposed to too much wind.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.570
It's all right, big sister.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.780
It's warm.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:18.700
When I do this, I remember those days.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:23.580
Weren't those the days?

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:38.800
That was close by.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:43.020
With this bad weather,
the roads are probably in bad shape.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:46.060
Perhaps even Rosette has given up.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:50.230
Trying to buy time uselessly?
Or perhaps you're hoping against hope?

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.190
I'd rather you call it parental affection.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:57.200
Four years ago, when I brought
her to the Magdalene Order...

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:02.240
No, since long before that, I've thought
of myself as that girl's guardian.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:05.000
I have a duty to protect her.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.080
That's why...

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.960
I can't just hand her over
without offering any resistance!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:20.760
Up there?

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.970
Oh, there you are,
there you are, Minister Remington!

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:26.390
I'm late, but I'm here to get you!

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:34.530
Nice to meet you, Sister Rosette.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:38.110
We have also come to get you.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:40.160
Lord Joshua is waiting.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:42.530
Joshua?!

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:51.750
What's going on?!
What do you mean, Joshua is waiting?!

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:54.750
Hey!

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.420
Say something!

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:01.800
What?

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:07.680
Above you!

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.600
The second skylight on the east side!

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.410
Rosette...

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.450
Minister Remington, what's going on?

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.290
Just now,
they said something about Joshua.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:29.330
For now, let's get out of here.

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:32.330
Oh my, what an appalling older sister.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:35.250
I wonder what
Lord Joshua would say if he saw you?

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.960
Who are you?!

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:41.340
Please call me
a puppet master, Sister Rosette.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:45.140
A puppet master?
You can't mean that these people are...

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:46.010
Yes.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:49.100
But it's all right. They're just unconscious.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:52.770
But they're such helpless marionettes.

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:57.270
If I so desire... You understand, don't you?

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:00.650
Sister, please, save me.

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:03.360
Oh, merciful Sister...

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:06.280
I'm scared, Mama.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:13.330
You, who are of the clergy, will not stand by
and watch these poor unfortunate lambs,

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:16.420
who just happened to
be here, be killed, will you?

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.710
What do you want?!

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:24.090
It's all up to your soul.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:29.140
If you obey without question,
then their lives will be saved.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.720
Don't listen, Rosette!

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:34.270
The train will be here soon.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:37.480
If you get on board,
you can go to where Lord Joshua is.

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:39.900
It's just Aion's trap!

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.070
Aion!

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:48.780
That's not it.
This is what Lord Joshua desires.

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:51.120
He says he really wants to see his older sister.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:56.040
Hurry up and go to
see him. Lord Joshua is waiting.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.960
He looks like he's in a lot of pain.

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:00.500
He's suffering so much he can't even eat.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:01.710
Joshua...

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:10.390
Tell me! Where's Joshua? Where is he?!

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:12.770
Is it true that he's suffering?!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:17.440
Please, let me see Joshua!

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.860
Calm down, Rosette

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.650
Minister Remington!

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:25.320
Sister Rosette, he wishes for you alone.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:27.860
We will have the Minister wait here.

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:31.410
Please come with us, Sister.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:35.250
You're the only one who can
save Lord Joshua from his suffering.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.080
Rosette!

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:52.850
I'm sorry, Minister Remington.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.060
What happened this time?

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:00.730
I broke the dish.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:04.400
That's Sister Kate's teacup!

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:09.570
But I can't believe the handle just fell off.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.910
Hello, this is the Magdalene Order.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:17.910
What? Shots fired?
At Grand Central Station?

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:19.250
I understand.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.290
As you get new information,
please contact me again.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.300
You two...

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:33.430
What about Grand Central Station?

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:43.270
Sister Rosette, you are truly a wise person.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:54.240
I'm certain that Lord Joshua
will be delighted as well.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.160
What's the matter?

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:36.080
The train will be leaving soon.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.130
...Rosette!

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.630
Minister Remington...

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:48.920
Joshua is...

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.050
Minister Remington!

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:53.720
What a troublesome person.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:56.930
After all that's happened,
he is still trying to interfere.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:16:00.350
Out of respect for his
older sister, I tried showing mercy.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:04.480
I have no choice. I'll have you die here!

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:05.860
Remington!

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:14.110
Minister Remington!

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.130
Rosette!

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.140
Minister Remington!

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:47.400
Minister Remington, I'm sorry! I...

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.900
We can talk later!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.610
I won't let you.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.780
I've grown tired of you.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:17:00.160
And all I was trying to do was take you
to where your beloved younger brother is.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:03.620
Why do you defy me, Sister Rosette?

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:09.170
I was a fool to fall for the honeyed
words of someone as cowardly as you!

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:12.880
Oh, so you don't want to see Lord Joshua?

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.340
Of course I want to see him!

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:16.760
Rosette!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.180
I want to see him.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:22.270
I want to fly to him immediately.

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:25.600
If he's coughing, I want to pat his back.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:28.440
If he's in pain,
then I want to take his place!

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:32.780
Of course you do. You are
the only one who can save Lord Joshua.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:36.110
And that's why I won't accept your help!

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:39.700
That's right,
I'm the only one who can save him.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:43.160
I will rescue Joshua
from you guys, no matter what!

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:44.370
Then you leave me no choice.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:47.920
In that case, I will make you
come with me, even by force!

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.380
Rosette, aim for their necks!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:02.640
With this many people as your opponents,
what can a little girl like you do?

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.530
Rosette, are you all right?

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:19.530
Yes!

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:26.580
I won't let you get away!

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:29.420
Rosette!

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:35.960
Minister Remington!

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:43.050
Rosette!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.480
This is...

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:54.520
A crucifix barrier!

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:59.070
Rosette!

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.070
Chrono...

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.240
Are you all right?

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:04.950
I put down too many crucifixes.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.830
Azmaria...

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.620
Rosette!

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.830
Chrono, you bastard!

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:15.050
You haven't changed, Rizel.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:17.880
Your methods are disgusting.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:23.220
Shut up. Your unsightly
form is fitting for a dog of God.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.390
Why, you!

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:30.230
An unexpected intrusion
has come up, Sister Rosette.

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:33.060
I'm sorry that I could not take you.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:36.150
Let us meet again some other time.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.220
You were so reckless.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:06.680
Couldn't you wait
a little longer until we showed up?

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:11.480
She said that Joshua was suffering.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:16.730
His body is weak after all.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:24.450
I'm sorry.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:32.540
I'll rescue him, no matter what.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:41.970
Rosette...

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:42.920
What's this?

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:45.140
I think you need to see this.

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:50.100
These papers were in
their hands once, so they're not reliable,

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.890
but they can probably serve as clues.

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:58.190
We've been searching for four years,

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:02.150
and a few months ago,
we finally spotted him.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:03.570
Joshua...
